 Industrials peers: P/E 15.3 vs 24.1, EV/EBITDA 10.1 vs 13.4 and P/FCF 12.1 vs 22.9 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 26% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 8.2% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 7.3% (vs the 8% bar).","The 4 covering analysts target $110 on average, 35% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 8% earns above the cost of capital of 8.1%, but the 0pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have been steady (CV 0.16).","It converts 6% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.55x.","ROE of 9% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.0x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.9% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.9x net debt to EBITDA ($5.3M of cash against $401.4M of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 4.7x.","Goodwill makes up 61% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 1.7% over 3 years, 4.4% over 5 years and 5.2% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 26% of profits supports about 2.1% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -5.0% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: a backlog worth 82% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 77%.","Capex runs only 0.4x depreciation (1.2% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 10, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.9%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 3 purchases and 5 sales over the past year, net $1.4M sold.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.7% (0.7% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.0% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 6,972 employees, each generates about $269K of revenue, 0.7x the Industrials median, and revenue has grown 5.9% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $17K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.1M (8x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":76,"head":"Invest: trades 52% below fair value of $170; p/E 15.3x vs sector 24.1x.","pros":["Composite 46, above the 39 line (gates 12/25)","Trades 52% below fair value of $170","P/E 15.3x vs sector 24.1x","EV/EBITDA 10.1x vs sector 13.4x","P/FCF 12.1x vs sector 22.9x"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":144.68,"vc":{"base":170.21,"base_src":"dcf","bear":128.73,"bull":226.22,"alt_median":52.28,"n_alt":3,"gap":2.2556,"dispersion":0.4562,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (46% dispersion)","DCF is 226% above the other models' median ($52.28)"]},"med":{"pe":24.0501,"ev_ebitda":13.39,"pfcf":22.9066,"pb":2.9489,"roic":0.0996,"gross_margin":0.2855,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0143}},"mc_quantiles":[104.47,119.63,128.73,138.16,143.5,148.12,153.53,158.19,162.18,167.38,171.31,175.34,180.22,186.72,191.76,197.46,206.38,215.16,226.22,247.0,281.32],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.535,"discount_rate":0.359,"terminal_growth":0.036,"exit_multiple":0.07},"ticker":"ICFI","date":"2026-11-13"}